lina 27599; email: dgshen@med.unc.edu."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Brain and Cognitive Engineering, Korea University, Seoul 02841, Republic of Korea; email: hisuk@korea.ac.kr."}]}}, {"fullName": "Wu G", "lastName": "Wu", "firstName": "Guorong", "initials": "G", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Radiology, University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill, North Carolina 27599; email: dgshen@med.unc.edu."}]}}, {"fullName": "Suk HI", "lastName": "Suk", "firstName": "Heung-Il", "initials": "HI", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7019-8962"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Brain and Cognitive Engineering, Korea University, Seoul 02841, Republic of Korea; email: hisuk@korea.ac.kr."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7019-8962"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics"]}, "journalInfo": {"volume": "19", "journalIssueId": 2569929, "dateOfPublication": "2017 Jun", "monthOfPublication": 6, "yearOfPublication": 2017, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Annu Rev Biomed Eng", "title": "Annual review of biomedical engineering", "essn": "1545-4274", "issn": "1523-9829", "isoabbreviation": "Annu Rev Biomed Eng", "nlmid": "100883581"}, "printPublicationDate": "2017-06-01"}, "pubYear": "2017", "pageInfo": "221-248", "abstractText": "This review covers computer-assisted analysis of images in the field of medical imaging. Recent advances in machine learning, especially with regard to deep learning, are helping to identify, classify, and quantify patterns in medical images. At the core of these advances is the ability to exploit hierarchical feature representations learned solely from data, instead of features designed by hand according to domain-specific knowledge. Deep learning is rapidly becoming the state of the art, leading to enhanced performance in various medical applications. We introduce the fundamentals of deep learning methods and review their successes in image registration, detection of anatomical and cellular structures, tissue segmentation, computer-aided disease diagnosis and prognosis, and so on. We conclude by discussing research issues and suggesting future directions for further improvement.", "affiliation": "Department of Radiology, University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill, North Carolina 27599; email: dgshen@med.unc.edu.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "K01 AG049089", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIBIB NIH HHS", "acronym": "EB", "grantId": "R01 EB006733", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIBIB NIH HHS", "acronym": "EB", "grantId": "R01 EB008374", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDCR NIH HHS", "acronym": "DE", "grantId": "R01 DE022676", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIMH NIH HHS", "acronym": "MH", "grantId": "R01 MH100217", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R01 AG042599", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "RF1 AG053867", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R01 AG049371", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIMH NIH HHS", "acronym": "MH", "grantId": "R21 MH108914", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R01 AG041721", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIBIB NIH HHS", "acronym": "EB", "grantId": "R01 EB009634", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Image Interpretation, Computer-Assisted", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Diagnostic Imaging", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majo